# Sources

Generated by {{skill_name}} v{{skill_version}}.

Record publications, public documentation, interviews, datasets, code, models, and other external inputs in proportion to their intended use.

For each material source, capture enough of the following to reconstruct the research:

- stable title or identifier;
- author, publisher, or owner;
- URL, DOI, repository, version, or commit when applicable;
- access date when the source may drift;
- intended use: cite, inspect, execute, incorporate, or redistribute;
- relevant limitations or unresolved questions.

Citation-only material does not require a source-ingestion gate. Stronger licence and provenance evidence becomes relevant when material is copied, adapted, committed, packaged, or redistributed.
